// `expose fn` gives a function an exported C-ABI symbol (KAMA_EXPORT) so a host can resolve it:
// `dlsym` on a --shared lib, and on wasm a real export in the module — `WebAssembly.Module.exports()`
// lists `expose_basic_add` (a loose file's symbols are qualified by its file name, as a module's are
// by its module path), and an embedder that instantiates the .wasm directly can call it without
// running `main` at all. It stays an ordinary function to kama callers, called by its kama name.
//
// ⚠️ It is NOT reachable as `Module._expose_basic_add` off the generated JS, which an earlier version of this
// comment claimed. Measured 2026-08-23: that needs -sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS/-sMODULARIZE, which kama
// does not emit — the generated .js is a PROGRAM (shebang, runs main, exits), not a library. The
// richer module-export surface is ROADMAP §7 (2.0) work.
expose fn int32 add(int32 a, int32 b)
{
    return a + b;
}

fn int32 main()
{
    return add(a: 40, b: 2);
}
